Package: listsr
Title: Find Pattern in the Lists You Already Collect
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("K. W.", "Bridges", email = "kim.bridges@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Claude (Anthropic)", role = "aut"))
Description: A small toolkit for turning the ragged, everyday lists people
    already keep (sites, and the items found at each) into reproducible groups.
    It reads ragged list text into a binary two-way table, scans frequencies,
    measures Jaccard dissimilarity, draws dendrograms (optionally coloured by
    external metadata), and cuts a tree into groups by the "most variable site
    sets the line" assessment-line rule. It is the companion engine to the
    'lists' document and shares lineage with the 'coenosr' package, which reads
    Braun-Blanquet releve files.
